WEBVTT

00:00:27.111 --> 00:00:29.947
Oh, you're still here, Your Majesty.

00:00:30.198 --> 00:00:32.241
Vasant.

00:00:32.491 --> 00:00:36.412
You knew my mother, didn't you?

00:00:36.662 --> 00:00:43.169
Yes. Augusta Farahnéz
was a truly wonderful woman.

00:00:43.419 --> 00:00:46.172
She held fast to her noble ambitions,

00:00:46.422 --> 00:00:50.176
always had a smile on her face,
and was filled with affection.

00:00:50.426 --> 00:00:55.514
She seemed like a goddess to us
when we were child soldiers.

00:01:01.229 --> 00:01:07.818
<i>Soko ni nani ga aru toshite mo</i>

00:01:08.069 --> 00:01:16.494
<i>Mikai no ryouiki e kimi to</i>

00:01:24.752 --> 00:01:32.802
<i>Mijikai yume wo miteta ima</i>

00:01:33.052 --> 00:01:37.431
<i>Are wa kimi no senaka</i>

00:01:37.682 --> 00:01:43.604
<i>Kako? Mirai?</i>

00:01:43.854 --> 00:01:54.365
<i>Furikitte iru meetaa no hari wo mushi shite</i>

00:01:54.615 --> 00:01:57.493
<i>Oikaze to kanjou no muku hou e</i>

00:01:57.743 --> 00:02:03.666
<i>Habataku tabi kizukasareru</i>

00:02:03.916 --> 00:02:09.213
<i>Nido to deaenai sora ga aru koto</i>

00:02:09.463 --> 00:02:14.719
<i>Sore demo tobitatsu nara</i>

00:02:14.969 --> 00:02:21.517
<i>Kimi no tsubasa ni naru watashi ga</i>

00:02:55.968 --> 00:02:58.721
Where the heck did they wander off to?

00:02:58.971 --> 00:03:00.222
Atamora!

00:03:00.473 --> 00:03:03.726
I found something you should see!

00:03:03.976 --> 00:03:05.144
Here.

00:03:05.394 --> 00:03:08.898
"Turan forms a refugee government..."

00:03:09.148 --> 00:03:11.484
Yahoo!

00:03:19.784 --> 00:03:24.455
With any luck, this will bring a
little hope to the people of Turan...

00:03:24.705 --> 00:03:29.668
Just knowing you're alive
will make them happy for sure!

00:03:29.919 --> 00:03:31.128
Fam...

00:03:31.379 --> 00:03:36.217
The Grand Race is still waiting!
Let's get moving!

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:43.766
Finally halfway there...

00:03:46.852 --> 00:03:50.356
Transport of the Sky Pirate battleship
fleet will commence shortly.

00:03:50.606 --> 00:03:53.609
All transport personnel, please gather on deck.

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:00.157
Take a northbound detour.

00:04:00.408 --> 00:04:02.952
The Federation's 1st Fleet
is still prowling about.

00:04:03.202 --> 00:04:04.120
R°gefl

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:08.416
There won't be any problems
with me along for the ride, though!

00:04:08.666 --> 00:04:10.501
Give the people of Anatoray my regards.

00:04:10.751 --> 00:04:12.545
Sure.

00:04:12.795 --> 00:04:16.382
I'm impressed they managed
to gather so many so quickly...

00:04:16.632 --> 00:04:21.011
Oh, yes. Have you heard anything
about a so-called "Grand Race"?

00:04:21.262 --> 00:04:26.183
Yeah. It apparently took place
long before we returned.

00:04:26.434 --> 00:04:27.268
Why do you ask?

00:04:27.518 --> 00:04:30.729
Oh, I've just been hearing
the name a lot lately...

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:33.107
"Anatoray"...?

00:04:33.357 --> 00:04:35.651
Oh, are you alone?

00:04:35.901 --> 00:04:36.902
Yes.

00:04:37.153 --> 00:04:41.574
I need to find a new target for us.

00:04:41.824 --> 00:04:45.161
It must be rough,
being dragged into all of this...

00:04:46.704 --> 00:04:51.834
No. A navi's job is to stick with his or her pilot.

00:04:52.084 --> 00:04:55.504
Having a reckless pilot makes life difficult...

00:04:55.754 --> 00:04:57.339
...as we can both attest to.

00:04:58.757 --> 00:05:01.844
Sometimes it's important
to say what's on your mind.

00:05:02.094 --> 00:05:06.640
Otherwise you'll both lose your way.

00:05:11.687 --> 00:05:16.108
This conference of allied nations has
been truly productive, Lady Vasant.

00:05:16.358 --> 00:05:19.653
Yes. The Augusta will certainly be pleased

00:05:19.904 --> 00:05:22.198
by the wise judgment your
nations have demonstrated.

00:05:22.448 --> 00:05:27.411
Unlike Turan, we aren't fools.

00:05:27.661 --> 00:05:31.207
As members of the Ades Federation,

00:05:31.457 --> 00:05:33.918
we will all work together to foster prosperity.

00:05:34.168 --> 00:05:37.546
Such is the true definition of world peace.

00:05:37.796 --> 00:05:41.133
The Augusta will never do anything
to betray the expectations

00:05:41.383 --> 00:05:46.347
of those ambitious subjects
who have rallied around her.

00:05:47.806 --> 00:05:53.312
It is truly reassuring that you, Lady Vasant,
are the Federation's contact representative.

00:05:53.562 --> 00:05:56.899
You are our beacon, after all.

00:05:57.149 --> 00:05:59.068
The "Amethyst of Chaos"...

00:05:59.318 --> 00:06:03.489
You're the scion of a southern nation that
was once a thorn in the Federation's side.

00:06:03.739 --> 00:06:07.243
To think that you're now a general
under the Augusta's direct command...

00:06:10.246 --> 00:06:15.000
The Chaos region hasn't been
called that in a very long time.

00:06:17.878 --> 00:06:22.299
It appears the returnees' kings have
scrambled to send emissaries here.

00:06:22.550 --> 00:06:24.718
It sounds like they hope
to ensure their own survival

00:06:24.969 --> 00:06:28.806
at the expense of their land and their people.

00:06:29.056 --> 00:06:32.226
I imagine they were horrified by Turan's demise.

00:06:32.476 --> 00:06:34.812
I realize he was dealing with returnees,

00:06:35.062 --> 00:06:38.607
but that former bodyguard
couldn't be any more coldhearted.

00:06:38.857 --> 00:06:42.069
Just how far must that bloodthirsty
upstart expand the battle lines

00:06:42.319 --> 00:06:45.364
until he's satisfied?!

00:06:45.614 --> 00:06:48.867
When you get right down to it,
he's nothing but a guard

00:06:49.118 --> 00:06:52.413
who has the young Augusta
wrapped around his little finger...

00:06:52.663 --> 00:06:55.291
Sadri will head from the
Corbeau Peninsula to Batos.

00:06:55.541 --> 00:06:57.835
Kayvén will go to Rhaetus.

00:06:58.085 --> 00:06:59.962
(_)rang will go to Ta Opisthen.

00:07:00.212 --> 00:07:02.298
And Sorfish will head to Boreas.

00:07:02.548 --> 00:07:06.302
They're all bountiful lands, with lots of wheat.

00:07:06.552 --> 00:07:10.889
And doesn't Boreas have
Claudia deposits as well?

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:16.020
That's correct, Augusta!
You're very knowledgeable indeed!

00:07:16.270 --> 00:07:18.522
Vasant taught me.

00:07:18.772 --> 00:07:23.152
I need to hurry and become
a great Augusta like Mother.

00:07:23.402 --> 00:07:28.657
So that everyone can live richer, happier lives.

00:07:28.907 --> 00:07:30.367
You have a heart of gold.

00:07:30.618 --> 00:07:37.374
I, Sorfish, shall risk life and limb to
fulfill my duty to recapture territory!

00:07:37.625 --> 00:07:41.003
Hey! Say something too!

00:07:41.253 --> 00:07:46.759
Unlike you, I speak with results,
not with long-winded bravado.

00:07:47.009 --> 00:07:49.386
Please be careful and return safely, both of you.

00:07:49.637 --> 00:07:54.141
Especially you, SorGsh. Don't get
too friendly with the girls, okay?

00:07:55.267 --> 00:07:59.647
Firang! What did you tell the Augusta?!

00:07:59.897 --> 00:08:01.732
Luscinia!

00:08:04.610 --> 00:08:06.654
Everything is set.

00:08:06.904 --> 00:08:09.490
Preparations are in place to conquer each land.

00:08:09.740 --> 00:08:12.284
Then we begin tonight, as planned.

00:08:12.534 --> 00:08:16.455
Also, I came across this
in former Turan territory.

00:08:16.705 --> 00:08:19.166
Tu ran refugee government?

00:08:19.416 --> 00:08:22.670
Only now does she make her move...

00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:28.050
Princess Millia may be destined for turmoil.

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:29.635
What?!

00:08:29.885 --> 00:08:34.181
My Ships are gone!

00:08:57.246 --> 00:09:03.252
"We've transported all the battleships
you've stolen to a safe location.

00:09:03.502 --> 00:09:07.423
You have seven battleships to go. Good luck."

00:09:07.673 --> 00:09:09.550
Where is this "safe location"?!

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:11.301
Fam...

00:09:11.552 --> 00:09:14.138
This is... quite a place.

00:09:14.388 --> 00:09:17.349
Yep. It's the Eldorado entertainment area.

00:09:18.350 --> 00:09:22.730
It's famous for the underground
Vanship races held here.

00:09:24.189 --> 00:09:27.025
We have a referral from Duke Bollner.

00:09:27.276 --> 00:09:30.320
All right! It's time to get rich!

00:09:30.571 --> 00:09:31.905
Let's have some fun today!

00:09:32.156 --> 00:09:36.118
You oughta hit the jackpot
and become a man too! Yeah!

00:09:53.385 --> 00:09:57.765
I take it you're Lady Roshanak Babar,
the Federation baroness?

00:09:59.850 --> 00:10:01.018
And you are...?

00:10:01.268 --> 00:10:04.146
Fam Fan Fan. A Vanship pilot.

00:10:04.396 --> 00:10:08.609
Oh? What does a Vanship pilot want with me?

00:10:08.859 --> 00:10:11.737
We're told that you're a
regular patron of Eldorado

00:10:11.987 --> 00:10:15.032
and that you're especially
interested in the Vanship races.

00:10:15.282 --> 00:10:19.787
Yes. I even have a participant
in today's main race.

00:10:20.037 --> 00:10:23.957
I would like to compete with this person...

00:10:24.208 --> 00:10:28.212
...for ownership of your
state battleship, the NéhTd!

00:10:40.224 --> 00:10:41.475
Sure.

00:10:41.725 --> 00:10:47.105
In exchange, if I win,
I get to keep this little cutie.

00:10:47.356 --> 00:10:48.190
Huh?!

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:53.278
I love pretty boys as much as I love gambling.

00:10:53.529 --> 00:10:56.615
And this one's very much my type.

00:10:56.865 --> 00:10:59.451
You're going to accept
another such bet, milady?

00:10:59.701 --> 00:11:03.956
Oh, Lady Roshanak. You certainly
do have a fondness for them...

00:11:09.294 --> 00:11:10.963
Yes! She took the bait!

00:11:11.213 --> 00:11:12.047
Fan'!

00:11:12.297 --> 00:11:14.883
Don't tell me that's why
you had me dress this way?!

00:11:15.133 --> 00:11:19.263
Don't sweat it. The races
here are low-level stuff.

00:11:19.513 --> 00:11:21.765
--Right?
--Yes, I guess...

00:11:22.015 --> 00:11:23.725
Yashbal!

00:11:23.976 --> 00:11:26.562
You called, Mistress?

00:11:26.812 --> 00:11:28.397
Yashbal Anand?!

00:11:28.647 --> 00:11:30.858
No way! What is he doing here?!

00:11:31.108 --> 00:11:31.984
Gisey?

00:11:32.234 --> 00:11:36.613
H-He was a pilot in the Grand Race...

00:11:38.282 --> 00:11:39.867
You're very well-informed.

00:11:40.117 --> 00:11:45.539
Indeed, Yashbal here was
in the Grand Race finals.

00:11:45.789 --> 00:11:50.711
In Eldorado, though, he's only
known as the "Unbeatable Falcon."

00:11:50.961 --> 00:11:53.088
Wha...?! That's not fair, using a fake name!

00:11:53.338 --> 00:11:57.301
Incidentally, he hasn't lost
once out of 120 races.

00:12:03.765 --> 00:12:05.851
I'll never forgive you if you lose!

00:12:12.858 --> 00:12:17.321
It's a twenty-lap speed race
over a ten-mile-long course.

00:12:17.571 --> 00:12:21.867
Meaning it'll last two hours or so, I guess...

00:12:22.117 --> 00:12:26.204
That final deceleration point will be the key.

00:12:26.455 --> 00:12:30.792
We can also assume our opponent
knows the course inside and out.

00:12:31.043 --> 00:12:33.545
A Grand Race finalist, huh?

00:12:33.795 --> 00:12:36.423
He's gonna be one tough customer.

00:12:36.673 --> 00:12:43.555
He'll be very difficult to beat if he's
remained an active racer all this time,

00:12:43.805 --> 00:12:46.016
unlike Dad and the Sky Pirates.

00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:53.899
But we have another Grand Race to hold, right?

00:13:20.175 --> 00:13:23.136
Oh! Here we go!

00:13:23.387 --> 00:13:25.555
We'll make our move during the final lap.

00:13:25.806 --> 00:13:30.519
Until then, we can stay behind him,
and even fall behind at the bottleneck--

00:13:30.769 --> 00:13:32.020
just don't lose him.

00:13:32.270 --> 00:13:35.899
Roger. I'll leave the timing to you.

00:13:53.959 --> 00:13:55.419
Fam...!

00:14:04.261 --> 00:14:07.097
So this is what a Grand Race
competitor is like!

00:14:19.401 --> 00:14:22.404
Whoa! He's got a huge lead over 'em all!

00:14:31.663 --> 00:14:33.415
H-He's going to crash!

00:14:33.665 --> 00:14:36.209
He's got guts, and he ain't afraid to show it!

00:14:39.212 --> 00:14:42.966
Man, he really is good! No one's even close!

00:14:51.516 --> 00:14:53.143
Worried?

00:14:54.561 --> 00:14:59.399
No. Fam won't lose. I know it.

00:14:59.649 --> 00:15:05.197
Say. Have you heard the rumors
about the Turan refugee government?

00:15:06.448 --> 00:15:10.202
It's all everyone's talking about,
wherever you go.

00:15:10.452 --> 00:15:13.205
I can't believe they still insist on resisting

00:15:13.455 --> 00:15:15.332
after the way the Federation
thoroughly destroyed Turan.

00:15:15.582 --> 00:15:17.959
Such things are beyond--
I don't understand stuff like that.

00:15:18.210 --> 00:15:20.504
Everyone's saying how ridiculous it is.

00:15:35.143 --> 00:15:38.480
Greedy only for your own rights and interests,

00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:41.900
you have, to this day, used your
status to line your pockets

00:15:42.150 --> 00:15:47.489
and commit countless crimes against the state.

00:15:47.739 --> 00:15:52.369
Moreover, reports state that you have
willingly given battleships you own

00:15:52.619 --> 00:15:58.792
to former Princess Millia of Turan
and assisted in her uprising.

00:15:59.042 --> 00:16:03.171
Today's announcement of
Turan's refugee government

00:16:03.421 --> 00:16:06.007
was only made possible through your help.

00:16:06.258 --> 00:16:10.137
Th-That's absurd! You think <i>we</i> assisted Turan?!

00:16:10.387 --> 00:16:16.685
O-Our battleships <i>were</i> stolen,
but that was the Sky Pirates' doing!

00:16:16.935 --> 00:16:19.312
These accusations are ludicrous!

00:16:19.563 --> 00:16:21.773
This is a royal order.

00:16:22.023 --> 00:16:24.234
You are hereby sentenced to death.

00:16:30.282 --> 00:16:32.868
Th-The Extermination Squad!

00:16:49.843 --> 00:16:52.095
He barely slowed down at all!

00:16:56.516 --> 00:16:57.976
Fan'!

00:17:00.854 --> 00:17:05.192
This brings back memories.
It's almost like the Grand Race itself.

00:17:05.442 --> 00:17:09.196
But, like everything else, it's a false veneer.

00:17:12.574 --> 00:17:16.912
Even these ladies were once
royalty of renowned kingdoms.

00:17:17.162 --> 00:17:23.043
They were given noble status in
exchange for their homelands and pride.

00:17:23.293 --> 00:17:25.295
As was I.

00:17:27.005 --> 00:17:30.926
"Forsake your kingdom and become
a lapdog," is what you're saying?

00:17:31.176 --> 00:17:35.263
Pride, responsibility... None of it really matters.

00:17:35.513 --> 00:17:43.730
Struggling tenaciously will only cause
more conflict and further bloodshed.

00:17:46.483 --> 00:17:48.026
It's meaningless.

00:17:54.282 --> 00:17:56.576
I disagree.

00:17:58.828 --> 00:18:04.960
I'd rather fight to the death than have
to live without pride and meaning.

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:17.472
Please behave yourselves.
It'll save trouble for us all.

00:18:17.722 --> 00:18:21.643
Those who sully the name of the Augusta
must not be allowed to escape!

00:18:26.314 --> 00:18:27.941
I can't keep "P!

00:18:29.526 --> 00:18:32.946
Just one lap left. He's got this in the bag!

00:18:33.196 --> 00:18:35.198
Come on, Fam! Get it in gear!

00:18:35.448 --> 00:18:37.284
Is this how it's gonna end?!

00:18:38.743 --> 00:18:40.412
Gisey! How far to the goal?!

00:18:40.662 --> 00:18:42.831
A quarter mile!

00:18:44.582 --> 00:18:46.960
All right! Cut the fuel!

00:18:47.210 --> 00:18:49.045
Please!

00:18:49.296 --> 00:18:50.839
I'm on it!

00:18:52.007 --> 00:18:53.591
Fam...

00:18:53.842 --> 00:18:56.428
Jettisoning left wired spear!

00:18:57.804 --> 00:19:01.683
Dumping all fuel, coolant, and Claudia reserves!

00:19:05.228 --> 00:19:09.024
--She dumped their fuel?!
--Huh? Huh?!

00:19:09.274 --> 00:19:11.526
She jettisoned it to lighten their ship!

00:19:11.776 --> 00:19:14.029
Not bad for a final gamble!

00:19:14.279 --> 00:19:17.449
But can she make the turn?!

00:20:00.658 --> 00:20:03.286
I refuse to lose!

00:20:05.413 --> 00:20:07.374
Oh, no! They're gonna crash!

00:20:07.624 --> 00:20:09.167
Now!

00:20:43.910 --> 00:20:45.954
Sh-She actually did it!

00:20:46.204 --> 00:20:47.372
Hooray!

00:20:47.622 --> 00:20:50.542
Dammit! I lost it all...!

00:20:55.296 --> 00:20:56.464
Fan'!

00:20:56.714 --> 00:20:59.134
--Fam! Fam!
--Millia!

00:20:59.384 --> 00:21:03.680
Fam! Don't scare me like that ever again...!

00:21:03.930 --> 00:21:07.600
Sorry! But do you think better of me now?

00:21:07.851 --> 00:21:10.812
It was incredible! It took my breath away!

00:21:11.062 --> 00:21:14.232
It was almost like an actual Grand Race!

00:21:16.734 --> 00:21:19.237
Curse you! You lousy ex-bodyguard...!

00:21:28.079 --> 00:21:32.125
How can you do this?! Have you
forgotten Lady Farahn5z's ardent wish?!

00:21:32.375 --> 00:21:35.545
Granting Lady Farahn5z's wish...

00:21:36.671 --> 00:21:38.631
...requires...

00:21:40.425 --> 00:21:42.218
...your blood.

00:21:43.470 --> 00:21:46.931
At daybreak, we officially announce to the world

00:21:47.182 --> 00:21:48.892
this purging in the name of the Augusta.

00:21:49.142 --> 00:21:50.643
Understood.

00:21:55.940 --> 00:21:59.986
I never imagined they would
negotiate that turn like that.

00:22:00.236 --> 00:22:05.533
My ineptitude has failed you.
You may punish me as you see fit.

00:22:05.783 --> 00:22:09.245
I'm sure this is for the best.

00:22:09.496 --> 00:22:12.040
The NihTd is hers to take.

00:22:13.708 --> 00:22:17.962
Unbelievable! None of you bet on me?!

00:22:18.213 --> 00:22:20.173
Why the heck not?!

00:22:20.423 --> 00:22:23.593
I'll have you know I'm the future champion!

00:22:23.843 --> 00:22:27.388
The future Grand Race champion! Got it?!

00:22:30.892 --> 00:22:36.481
<i>Sora wa dore hodo takai no darou</i>

00:22:36.731 --> 00:22:42.529
<i>Kaze wa dore hodo tsuyoi no darou</i>

00:22:42.779 --> 00:22:48.368
<i>Mizu wa dore hodo sunderu darou</i>

00:22:48.618 --> 00:22:55.667
<i>Kimi no mune no naka dewa</i>

00:22:56.876 --> 00:23:08.346
<i>Namida uketomeru
kimi no te no hira ni itsuka naritai</i>

00:23:08.596 --> 00:23:20.441
<i>Onaji kanashimi onaji kuuki wo wakeaitai</i>

00:23:20.692 --> 00:23:26.281
<i>lma hashiridasu fune no saki wo</i>

00:23:26.531 --> 00:23:35.081
<i>Tamerawazu kimi no muki e susumete</i>

00:23:35.331 --> 00:23:41.045
<i>Kaze no umi de hobashira wo tate</i>

00:23:41.296 --> 00:23:46.843
<i>Kumo no nami wo suberihajimeyou</i>

00:23:47.093 --> 00:23:52.599
<i>Tooi hoshi wo konpasu ni shite</i>

00:23:52.849 --> 00:24:00.523
<i>Kimi to mezasu kanata e</i>

00:24:03.901 --> 00:24:04.777
<i>What's wrong, Teddy?</i>

00:24:05.028 --> 00:24:08.906
<i>D-During that last race, lgnace and
the others talked me into, well...</i>

00:24:09.157 --> 00:24:10.867
<i>They made you make a bet, huh?</i>

00:24:11.117 --> 00:24:13.703
<i>--So I bet on you and Fam!
--Huh?</i>

00:24:13.953 --> 00:24:17.790
<i>And then the entire place went
into an uproar about a huge upset...</i>

00:24:18.041 --> 00:24:20.376
<i>What should I do with this ticket?</i>

00:24:20.627 --> 00:24:24.464
<i>--You haven't cashed it in yet?
--"Cashed in"? What's that?</i>

00:24:24.714 --> 00:24:26.257
<i>S-Someone! Stop the ship!</i>

00:24:26.507 --> 00:24:28.885
<i>We hafta go back to Eldorado right now!</i>
